+Key finding (cost-model directionality; changes the interpretation):
+- The repository's cost model prices every fill at `close + slippage_cents/100 +
+  close * slippage_proportional`, for buys and sells alike (`engine.py`; the
+  existing `tests/test_engine.py::test_short_side` asserts this contract). For a
+  long/short rule this makes sell-side fills FAVORABLE: a two-bar round trip with
+  `slippage_cents=2.0` only ends at exactly the initial equity (1,000,000.000000)
+  for both the long and the short round trip, i.e. slippage has zero net cost.
+- AMZN full-sample (lookback 5, 4451 fills over 4465 bars): zero total return
+  +5.537258; slippage-only +5.539447 (slightly better than zero); commission-only
